# .kiroignore — workspace ignore file for the Kiro CLI (V3 agent harness).
#
# Scope: in CLI V3, this file only filters content-search and
# filename-search results (fuzzy file lookup, grep-style search). It does
# NOT reduce the startup context/token baseline, and it does NOT affect any
# other CLI tool. It has no effect on the IDE (`kiroAgent.agentIgnoreFiles`
# is a separate, IDE-only setting).
#
# `driftcheck`, `docsync`, `ctxbudget`, and the other Python tools under
# tools/ read the filesystem directly and are UNAFFECTED by this file. Do
# not assume an entry here hides anything from governance tooling, CI, or
# git — it only trims noise from interactive search results.
#
# Deliberately NOT ignored (do not add these — see task context):
#   - .kiro/skills/kiro-cli-reference/references/
#   - .kiro/skills/claude-prompting-reference/references/
#   - .kiro/skills/agent-creation/references/agentskills/
#     Vendored doc mirrors — specialist agents grep these as their only
#     route to Kiro/Claude documentation.
#   - tmp/
#     Holds generated reports (e.g. tmp/context-budget-report.md) agents
#     read as part of their work.

# --- Build and environment noise ---
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
node_modules/

# --- Secrets (defense in depth; mirrors agent fs_read deny rules) ---
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
config.toml
secrets/
